#!/bin/bash
# Auto-formats staged C++, YAML, Lua, TOML, Python, shell, CMake and PowerShell
# files. CI's format checks remain the actual gate if a local formatter is
# missing or the hook is bypassed with --no-verify.

staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR)

cxx_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '^(src|tests)/.*\.(cpp|h)$' || true)
if [[ -n "${cxx_files}" ]]; then
  if command -v clang-format >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "${cxx_files}" | while IFS= read -r f; do
      clang-format -i "${f}" || exit $?
      git add "${f}" || exit $?
    done
  else
    echo "pre-commit: clang-format not found on PATH - skipping C++" \
      "formatting (CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi

yaml_files=$(echo "${staged}" \
  | grep -E '(^\.yamlfmt$|^\.yamllint$|\.(yaml|yml)$)' \
  | grep -vE '^charts/augustad/templates/' \
  | grep -vE '^clusters/onprem/flux-system/gotk-components\.yaml$' || true)
if [[ -n "${yaml_files}" ]]; then
  if command -v yamlfmt >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "${yaml_files}" | while IFS= read -r f; do
      yamlfmt "${f}" || exit $?
      git add "${f}" || exit $?
    done
  else
    echo "pre-commit: yamlfmt not found on PATH - skipping YAML formatting" \
      "(CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi

lua_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '\.lua$' || true)
if [[ -n "${lua_files}" ]]; then
  if command -v stylua >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "${lua_files}" | while IFS= read -r f; do
      stylua "${f}" || exit $?
      git add "${f}" || exit $?
    done
  else
    echo "pre-commit: stylua not found on PATH - skipping Lua formatting" \
      "(CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi

toml_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '\.toml$' || true)
if [[ -n "${toml_files}" ]]; then
  if command -v taplo >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "${toml_files}" | while IFS= read -r f; do
      taplo fmt "${f}" 2>/dev/null || exit $?
      git add "${f}" || exit $?
    done
  else
    echo "pre-commit: taplo not found on PATH - skipping TOML formatting" \
      "(CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi

# Python, shell, CMake and Markdown, by the formatters uv runs at the versions
# CI pins.
python_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '\.py$' || true)
shell_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '(\.sh$|^\.githooks/)' || true)
cmake_files=$(echo "${staged}" \
  | grep -E '(^|/)CMakeLists\.txt$|\.cmake$' | grep -v '^third_party/' || true)
markdown_files=$(echo "${staged}" \
  | grep -E '\.md$' | grep -vE '^(third_party/|CHANGELOG\.md$)' || true)
if [[ -n "${python_files}${shell_files}${cmake_files}${markdown_files}" ]]; then
  if command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    # One argument per file; tracked paths have no spaces.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    {
      [[ -z "${python_files}" ]] \
        || uv tool run ruff@0.16.10 format --quiet ${python_files}
    } || exit $?
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    {
      [[ -z "${shell_files}" ]] \
        || uv tool run --from shfmt-py==4.2.0 shfmt -w ${shell_files}
    } || exit $?
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    {
      [[ -z "${cmake_files}" ]] \
        || uv tool run gersemi@0.29.2 --quiet -i ${cmake_files}
    } || exit $?
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    {
      [[ -z "${markdown_files}" ]] \
        || uv tool run --from nodejs-wheel==24.19.0 npx --yes prettier@3.9.9 \
          --log-level warn --write ${markdown_files}
    } || exit $?
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    git add ${python_files} ${shell_files} ${cmake_files} ${markdown_files} \
      || exit $?
  else
    echo "pre-commit: uv not found on PATH - skipping Python, shell, CMake" \
      "and Markdown formatting (CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi

# PowerShell, by PSScriptAnalyzer's formatter: Windows PowerShell on Windows,
# PowerShell 7 (pwsh) elsewhere. What PSScriptAnalyzer finds besides is
# pre-push's to stop, so its exit status is not this hook's.
powershell_files=$(echo "${staged}" | grep -E '\.ps1$' || true)
if [[ -n "${powershell_files}" ]]; then
  case "$(uname -s)" in
    MINGW* | MSYS* | CYGWIN*)
      powershell="powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass"
      ;;
    *)
      powershell=$(command -v pwsh >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo "pwsh -NoProfile")
      ;;
  esac
  if [[ -n "${powershell}" ]]; then
    # The command and its options; one argument per file.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    ${powershell} -File scripts/psscriptanalyzer.ps1 -Fix ${powershell_files} \
      >/dev/null
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    git add ${powershell_files} || exit $?
  else
    echo "pre-commit: pwsh not found on PATH - skipping PowerShell" \
      "formatting (CI will still catch this)." >&2
  fi
fi
